            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral glenohumeral septic arthritis secondary to retroperitoneal abscess.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>378-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Glenohumeral septic arthritis is rare and usually a result of Staphylococcus aureus infection. Gram-negative septic arthritis is on the increase and is usually associated with intraabdominal pathology. We present a case of bilateral E. Coli glenohumeral septic arthritis associated with retroperitoneal abscess and discuss pitfalls in diagnosis and management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
